<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gaius Claudius Pulcher (consul 177 BCE)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 167 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gaius <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/claudius">Claudius</a> Pulcher was a Roman politician and general who served as consul in 177 BCE. In that year he completed the conquest of the Histri in Istria, storming their stronghold of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nesactium">Nesactium</a>, after which the Histrian king Epulo took his own life, and he then campaigned against the Ligurians. He was censor in 169 BCE with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiberius">Tiberius</a> Sempronius Gracchus.</p></div>
